Z||000001||rockcrawl||11-28-2000||05:55 PM||||The syclone engine is about as much work to install as a V8, plus you have to deal with piping the turbo. The other 500hp race engine is probably a 90deg v6 as well. The only advantage these engines have over a v8 is that they weigh less. I'm sure Archie could supply at least most of the parts needed to put either one in a Fiero.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
